# This working directory holds participant data -- imaging, DICOMs, behavioural
# logs, fMRIPrep output. So this file denies everything by default and allows
# back only the code and documentation. A new data folder dropped in here is
# ignored automatically; a new *script* has to be allowed below before git will
# see it. That is the intended trade: forgetting to add a script is a nuisance,
# forgetting to exclude a scan is a disclosure.
#
# Check what would actually be committed with:
#     git add -A && git status --short
# and confirm with:
#     git ls-files

*

# --- allowed ---------------------------------------------------------------
!.gitignore
!README.md
!scripts/
!scripts/**/*.py
!scripts/**/*.sh

# --- never, even under scripts/ --------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Participant-identifying output. Listed explicitly as well as being covered by
# the deny-all above, so the intent survives anyone relaxing the rules.
bids/
dicoms/
derivatives/
behavioral/
fmriprep*/
*_events.tsv
participants.tsv
events_qc.csv
bids_validator_output*.txt
